    "body": "\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nFix gradient computation for `tf.signal.rfft` when `fft_length` is smaller than the input size.\r\n\r\nThe forward `rfft` op implicitly truncates the input to `fft_length`, but the gradient path assumes the full input length, resulting in a shape mismatch during backpropagation.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Changes Made\r\n\r\n* Fix gradient handling for `tf.signal.rfft` when `fft_length < input.shape[-fft_rank:]`\r\n* Add gradient test coverage for multiple `fft_length` cases\r\n\r\n\r\n## How to Reproduce Error\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport tensorflow as tf\r\n\r\nx = tf.random.uniform([1, 10])\r\n\r\nwith tf.GradientTape() as tape:\r\n  tape.watch(x)\r\n  y = tf.signal.rfft(x, fft_length=(5,))\r\n  loss = tf.reduce_sum(tf.abs(y))\r\n\r\ngrad = tape.gradient(loss, x)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Error Before Fix\r\n\r\n```text\r\nInvalidArgumentError: Incompatible shapes: [5] vs. [10]\r\n```",
