      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "Fixes #100332.\n\nThis PR resolves an `InvalidArgumentError: Incompatible shapes` crash in `keras.layers.Attention` when running on macOS Metal (GPU) backends.\n\n**The Issue:**\nThe Metal backend fails to implicitly broadcast the boolean mask (shape `[B, 1, Tv]`) to the attention scores (shape `[B, Tq, Tv]`) during subtraction, causing a shape mismatch error (e.g., `[32, 20, 10] vs [32, 10]`).\n\n**The Fix:**\nExplicitly broadcast the mask to the shape of the attention scores using `tf.broadcast_to` before applying the mask. This ensures the backend receives tensors of identical shapes, preventing the broadcasting failure.\n\n**Verification:**\nValidated that the explicit broadcast logic is correct and causes no regressions on standard CPU execution (unable to run Metal tests in CI, but the fix targets the known backend ambiguity).",
